G467.b:
⟪ἀντ-απο-δίδωμι⟫
(ἀντί, ἀποδίδωμι), [in LXX for ⁨שׁלם⁩ pi., ⁨גּמל⁩, ⁨שׁוּב⁩ hi., etc.;] ⟪to give back as an equivalent⟫, ⟪recompense⟫, ⟪requital⟫ (the ἀντί expressing the idea of full, complete return; v. Lft., Notes, 46);
⟪(a)⟫ in favourable sense: ⟦Luke 14:14|Lk 14:14⟧, ⟦Romans 11:35|Ro 11:35⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:9|I Th 3:9⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ in unfavourable sense: ⟦Romans 12:19|Ro 12:19⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 1:6|II Th 1:6⟧, ⟦Hebrews 10:30|He 10:30⟧.†

G468.b:
† ⟪ἀντ-από-δομα⟫, -τος, τό
(< ἀνταποδίδωμι), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨גְּמוּל⁩;] ( = cl. -δοσις, q.v.), ⟪requital⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ in favourable sense: ⟦Luke 14:12|Lk 14:12⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ in unfavourable sense: ⟦Romans 11:9|Ro 11:9⟧.†

G473.b:
⟪ἀντί⟫
(the ι is elided only in ἀνθ᾽ ὧν), prep. c. gen. (cf. MM, VGT, s.v.);
⟪1.⟫ prop, in local sense, ⟪over against⟫, ⟪opposite⟫, hence;
⟪2.⟫ ⟪instead of⟫, ⟪in place of⟫, ⟪for⟫ (Hom., etc.): ⟦Matthew 5:38|Mt 5:38⟧ ⟦Matthew 17:27|17:27⟧, ⟦Luke 11:11|Lk 11:11⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:15|I Co 11:15⟧, ⟦Hebrews 12:2|He 12:2⟧; c. artic. inf. (cl.), ⟦James 4:15|Ja 4:15⟧; of succession, ⟦Matthew 2:22|Mt 2:22⟧; χάριν ἀ. χάριτος, ⟦John 1:16|Jo 1:16⟧ (M, Pr., 100); of price in exchange, ⟦Hebrews 12:16|He 12:16⟧; λύτρον ἀ. πολλῶν, ⟦Matthew 20:28|Mt 20:28⟧, ⟦Mark 10:45|Mk 10:45⟧ (M, Pr., 105); of requital, ⟦Romans 12:17|Ro 12:17⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:15|I Th 5:15⟧, ⟦1 Peter 3:9|I Pe 3:9⟧ (cf. Wi 11:15); ἀνθ᾽ ὧν, ⟪because⟫, ⟦Luke 1:20|Lk 1:20⟧ ⟦Luke 19:44|19:44⟧, ⟦Acts 12:23|Ac 12:23⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:10|II Th 2:10⟧ (cl., LXX for ⁨אֲשֶׁר⁩ ⁨תַּחַת⁩); id. therefore (cl., LXX), ⟦Luke 12:3|Lk 12:3⟧; ἀ. τούτου (LXX for ⁨עַל־כֵּן⁩), ⟦Ephesians 5:31|Eph 5:31⟧. As a prefix, ἀντι- (before vowels ἀντ-, ἀνθ᾽-), denotes
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪over against⟫, ἀντιπέραν;
	⟪(b)⟫ co-operation, ἀντιβάλλειν;
	⟪(c)⟫ requital, ἀντιμισθία;
	⟪(d)⟫ opposition, ἀντίχριστος;
	⟪(e)⟫ substitution, ἀνθύπατος. Compounds of ἀ. usually govern dat. (Bl., § 37, 7).†

G478.b:
⟪ἀντι-καθ-ίστημι⟫,
[in LXX: ⟦Deuteronomy 31:21|De 31:21⟧ (⁨ענה⁩), ⟦Joshua 5:7|Jos 5:7⟧, ⟦Micah 2:8|Mi 2:8⟧ (⁨קוּם⁩)*;]
⟪1.⟫ causal in pres. impf. fut. and 1 aor.; ⟪to replace⟫, ⟪oppose⟫.
⟪2.⟫ Intrans. in pass. and 2 aor. act.;
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to supersede⟫;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to resist⟫: ⟦Hebrews 12:4|He 12:4⟧.†

G482.b:
⟪ἀντι-λαμβάνω⟫,
[freq. in LXX for ⁨חזק⁩ hi., ⁨תּמךְ⁩, etc;] ⟪to take instead of⟫ or ⟪in turn⟫. Mid., c. gen., ⟪to take hold of⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of persons, ⟪to help⟫ (v. MM, VGT, s.v.): ⟦Luke 1:54|Lk 1:54⟧, ⟦Acts 20:35|Ac 20:35⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of things, ⟪to partake of⟫: ⟦1 Timothy 6:2|I Ti 6:2⟧ (v. Field, Notes, 210; Cremer, 386; and cf. συν-αντιλαμβάνω).†

G499.b:
** ⟪ἀντί-τυπος⟫, -ον
(v.s. τύπος), [in LXX: ⟦Ezra 3:13|Es 3:13⟧ A*;]
⟪1.⟫ act. ⟪striking back⟫; metaph., ⟪resisting⟫, ⟪adverse⟫.
⟪2.⟫ Pass. ⟪struck back⟫; metaph., ⟪corresponding to⟫ (MM, VGT, s.v.);
	⟪(a)⟫ as impression of a seal or copy of an archetype (τύπος) (RV, like in pattern), ⟦Hebrews 9:24|He 9:24⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ as the reality (of which τύπος is the copy or adumbration) (RV, after a true likeness), ⟦1 Peter 3:21|I Pe 3:21⟧ (Cremer, 357).†
